# Planning Requirements

- When creating plans (using `mcp_create_plan`), always include a tree folder structure showing the directory hierarchy for all files that will be changed, created, or deleted.
- Mark files in the tree with clear visual indicators:
  - `[new]` for files that will be created
  - `[update]` for files that will be modified
  - `[delete]` for files that will be deleted
- Show the full directory path context so it's clear where files are located relative to the workspace root.
- The tree structure should be included in the plan's "Files to Create" or "Files to Modify" sections.
- Use standard tree notation (e.g., `├──`, `└──`, `│`) or simple indentation to show hierarchy.

Example format:

```text
packages/ai-edu-backend/
├── modules/
│   └── example/
│       ├── [new] service.ts
│       ├── [new] example.school-router.ts
│       └── [update] types.ts
└── router/
    └── [update] router.school.ts
```

- This helps visualize the impact of changes and ensures all affected directories are considered.
